        "original_id": "711a744a-1db0-5950-9400-07479dfaf4fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Oscar Wilde, Ken Russell\n- Works: Salome's Last Dance, Salome\n- Concepts: framing narrative, New Testament adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Oscar Wilde was an Irish writer who lived from 16 October 1854 to 30 November 1900.\n- Oscar Wilde wrote plays, fiction, essays, and poetry.\n- Oscar Wilde wrote the 1893 play \"Salome.\"\n- \"Salome's Last Dance\" features action that is mostly a verbatim performance of Oscar Wilde's 1893 play \"Salome.\"\n- Oscar Wilde's play \"Salome\" is based on a story from the New Testament.\n- Ken Russell wrote a framing narrative that is also included in \"Salome's Last Dance.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e20cecbe-555a-5767-bbb1-70ba831917e6",
        "text": "Page: Salome's Last Dance. Sentence: Although most of the action is a verbatim performance of Oscar Wilde's 1893 play \"Salome\", which is itself based on a story from the New Testament, there is also a framing narrative written by Russell himself.\nPage: Oscar Wilde. Sentence: Oscar Fingal O'Flahertie Wills Wilde (16 October 185430 November 1900) was a prolific Irish writer who wrote plays, fiction, essays, and poetry.",
